{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Since it's called intuition, it probably judges danger not on purpose but like a flashback.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
If a foresight loop arises that neither one can control...<PG>
The nerve cells of the brain exchange information through faint electric currents.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Normally this information processing takes place within one brain, but when a foresight loop arises, it is the same as two brains processing the same information.<PG>
Unstoppable flashbacks would go on, and on top of that, twice the usual information would pour into the brain.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Couldn't this be an extremely dangerous state?
{PAUSE ""}
